# 360° Video

Browser-side equirectangular 360° video player. Triggered from interactions (`video360.open`), fills the screen, plays one `.mp4`/`.webm` 360° clip at a time, and rotates the view with drag + device orientation. The Kit camera does not move while the overlay is open.

Parallel to the spatial-sound overlay: same iconGroup template shape, same per-session onboarding, same caption pipeline, same drag/orientation conventions. Render path is Three.js (vs Web Audio FOA for spatial sound).

---

## Pipeline

```
fetch(video file)            ─┐
  │                            ├─ <video> element (HTMLVideoElement)
  └─ optional VTT fetch + parse ┘     │
                                       └─ THREE.VideoTexture
                                            │
                                            └─ MeshBasicMaterial
                                                 │
                                                 └─ SphereGeometry, scale.x = -1
                                                      (rendered from inside)
```

`useVideoSphere` owns the entire Three.js scene. `Video360Overlay` is pure UI + gesture/orientation wiring + phase management. Drag and `useDeviceOrientation` deltas call `sphere.addRotation(dYaw, dPitch)`; the rAF tick converts spherical coords into a `camera.lookAt(target)` and renders.

---

## Mount-ordering rule

`THREE.VideoTexture` registers a `requestVideoFrameCallback` on its source `<video>` at construction time. If that video has no `src`, the callback chain never starts — setting `src` later does not repair it, and the sphere stays black.

**Rule**: the sphere host `<div>` must only render after `load()` has resolved. The hook exposes `isReady` for this; `Video360Overlay` gates the host on it:

```tsx
{isReady ? (
    <div ref={sphereHostRef} className="v360-sphere" ... />
) : (
    <div className="v360-loading"><span className="v360-loading-spinner" /></div>
)}
```

On warm reopen the browser HTTP cache makes `load()` resolve in ~1 frame. On cold start the spinner covers the download.

---

## Phase machine

```
open → onboarding ──"Start"──▶ player ──close──▶ unmount
        │                                 ▲
        └─── (skipped if hasOnboarded) ───┘
```

| Phase | What renders | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `onboarding` | Frosted card with `Phone360Icon`, title, description, "Start the experience" button | Shown once per `Video360Provider` lifetime. Description text changes when device orientation API is available. |
| `player` | Sphere host (gated on `isReady`) + transient title overlay (~3 s) + bottom controls | Auto-plays the moment `phase === 'player' && isReady` is true. |

Per-session onboarding is tracked on `Video360Context.hasOnboarded` (React state on the provider):

- First open in a streaming session shows the onboarding card.
- Subsequent opens within the same session land directly in `player`.
- Survives overlay close → reopen (the provider stays mounted).
- Resets on a full page reload (the provider re-mounts).
- Not synced through `worldStateSync`. For cross-reload persistence use `sessionStorage`/`localStorage`.

Same pattern is mirrored in `SpatialSoundContext.hasOnboarded`, independently.

