## Authoring a new 360° video

1. Drop the `.mp4` (or `.webm`) into `kit-app-template-main/source/data/nucleus/videos/`. Filename must start with `NN_` where `NN` is the unique numeric prefix (e.g. `2_horseshow_pitch.mp4`). Equirectangular projection (2:1 aspect ratio) required.
2. Add an empty `Xform` named `video_360_NN` to `kit-app-template-main/source/data/scenes/sublayers/video_360_locations_layer.usda` at the world position. Trailing number must match the video prefix exactly (current convention uses no leading zeros: `video_360_1`, `video_360_2`).
3. Add a per-location i18n block to all four locale files (`en.json`, `sv.json`, `fr.json`, `es.json`) under `interactions.icon_video_360_NN` with `greeting`, `title`, `subtitle`, `videoTitle`. `videoTitle` is displayed in the transient title overlay (`title` is fallback).
4. Optional: drop a `NN_<name>.vtt` next to the video (same `NN` prefix) for closed captions.
5. Done — no `interactions.json` edit. The single `icon_video_360` template auto-discovers the new Xform on next stage load.

Video and optional `.vtt` are resolved via the Vite `@nucleus-videos` glob on the frontend — no extra config.

