## i18n strings

| Scope | Path | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Fixed (overlay chrome) | `video360.label`, `video360.captions.{showCaptions,hideCaptions}`, `video360.onboarding.{title,description,descriptionDesktop,startButton}` | Same text for every 360° experience |
| Fixed (bubble label) | `video360.watchButton` | Templated `"Watch 360° video: {{title}}"`. Rendered by `IconBubbleOverlay` when `cfg.mediaType === 'video360'`; `{{title}}` filled with `t(cfg.videoTitle) \|\| t(cfg.title)`. |
| Per-location | `interactions.icon_video_360_NN.{greeting,title,subtitle,videoTitle}` | Synthesised by the iconGroup expander; `videoTitle` is the canonical display string |

Keep all four locales in sync — every key referenced by the synthesised entries must resolve in `en/sv/fr/es.json`.

**Rendering rule (transient title overlay)**: `Video360Overlay` displays `t(entry.videoTitle) || t(entry.title)` under the fixed `video360.label`. Both fields arrive as i18n keys, not literal text — the overlay translates them. Don't pre-resolve them upstream.

