## State flow

```
Kit                              Web
────                             ────
interaction triggered            ChatContext registers `video360.open` handler
  → video360.open(payload)       → video360.open({ id, videoUrl, videoTitle, ... })
                                       │
                                 Video360Context
                                  ├─ entry: Video360Entry            ← payload
                                  ├─ isOpen: boolean                 ← derived (entry !== null)
                                  ├─ hasOnboarded: boolean           ← per-session flag
                                  ├─ open(entry) / close()
                                  └─ markOnboarded()
                                       │
                                 Video360Overlay (renders when isOpen)
                                  ├─ phase = hasOnboarded ? player : onboarding
                                  ├─ load() → isReady
                                  └─ on phase===player && isReady → mount sphere + play
```

`Video360Context` lives in `web-viewer-sample-main/src/features/streaming/contexts/Video360Context.tsx`, provided in `StreamOnlyWindow.tsx` between `ControlProvider` and `ChatProvider`. See `react-contexts.mdc` for the full provider hierarchy.

Anything reacting to the overlay being open reads `useVideo360().isOpen` directly — not through `useControl()`.

