## Hide-the-icon side effect

When the overlay opens, `ChatContext` sends `avatarPrim.hide` for the bound icon prim and `npcMarkers.hide` for the marker overlay:

```ts
useEffect(() => {
    if (!stream.streamReady || !video360.isOpen) return;
    const primPath = video360.entry?.primPath;
    if (!primPath) return;
    sendMessage('avatarPrim.hide', { primPath });
    sendMessage('npcMarkers.hide', {});
    return () => {
        sendMessage('avatarPrim.show', { primPath });
        sendMessage('npcMarkers.show', {});
    };
}, [video360.isOpen, video360.entry?.primPath, stream.streamReady]);
```

Keeps the VR headset model from poking through the onboarding card and from being visible behind the sphere during playback.

---

## Layer hygiene

A given `video_360_NN` Xform must be defined in **exactly one** layer — `video_360_locations_layer.usda`. Authoring the same prim in `usd_edits.usda` or any stronger sublayer will silently win composition and override the position. Symptom: VR headset spawns at one elevation while the projectable arrows render at another. Search every sublayer for the prim name first if this divergence appears. Same convention as spatial sound.

---

## Lifecycle

- One renderer/scene per overlay open. The Three.js renderer, scene, mesh, geometry, material, texture, and `<video>` element are all torn down on overlay close (`useEffect` cleanup in `useVideoSphere`). On reopen everything is rebuilt from scratch.
- Pixel ratio is set from `window.devicePixelRatio` on mount. No dynamic resolution scaling — tweak in `useVideoSphere.mount()` if a low-end device struggles.
- `texture.colorSpace = THREE.SRGBColorSpace` is the only colour pipeline knob. Source videos authored in sRGB.
- Sphere geometry is `SphereGeometry(500, 60, 40)` — radius arbitrary (camera at origin), tessellation is enough that pole distortion isn't visibly faceted.

