## Extending

### Add a new 360° video
See "Authoring a new 360° video" above. No code changes.

### Title overlay dwell time
`TITLE_OVERLAY_HOLD_MS` constant in `Video360Overlay.tsx`.

### Drag sensitivity
`DRAG_SENSITIVITY` constant (degrees per CSS pixel) in `Video360Overlay.tsx`.

### Persist `hasOnboarded` across page reloads
Add `sessionStorage.getItem/setItem` in `Video360Context`'s `useState` initialiser and `markOnboarded`. Don't route through `worldStateSync`.

### Render captions in a different position
Use `.v360-captions` in `Video360Overlay.css` for position and `bottom` / `--with-controls` offsets. The short-viewport media query tweaks padding and spacing only; **font sizes** follow the same caption tokens as the videobook in all viewports (see `video-playback.mdc` § Caption size).

### Non-equirect projection (cubemap, fisheye, etc.)
Replace the `SphereGeometry` + `MeshBasicMaterial` block in `useVideoSphere.mount()`. `VideoTexture` itself is projection-agnostic. Cubemap source → `THREE.CubeTexture` + skybox material + custom UVs for the strip/tile layout.

